  "name": "International Tropical Mega Battle",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The International Tropical Mega Battle was a junior tournament held each August at the Hilton Hawaiian Village in Honolulu, which Pokumon calls the first of what became the World Championships. The 1999 event, from 24 to 27 August, brought together players from the United States and Japan; on its second day every player was given a matte, bilingual Exeggutor drawn by game designer Kouichi Ooyama, and a matte Imakuni? was handed out there too, its origin traced by collectors only in 2018.\n\nIn 2000, on 26 and 27 August, 42 children aged 11 to 14 from nine countries each got a bilingual Lucky Stadium set on a Hawaiian beach, also by Ooyama. In 2001, on 25 and 26 August, 23 players from 10 countries played the VS Shield Battle with the same 30-card deck, the Tyranitar half deck with Tropical Breeze in place of its Tyranitar and Darkness Energy. Its Clair's Mantine showed a Psychic resistance where it should resist Fighting, and the mistake caused first-round games to be replayed.",
